direction: right
owner_plan: Full owner graph before key publication
frozen_union: Unique thread and queue leases
priority_solve: Private constants / prefix join / cycle least closure
priority_commit: At most R key publications
retire_plan: Clear borrowed roots before work unlock
owner_plan -> frozen_union -> priority_solve -> priority_commit -> retire_plan

caller: Logical caller / full multi-shot wind and denv
root: Private frame-only root / denv false
physical: Thread.cont + break.Next
service: Fresh request service activation
park: THREAD_PARK / no payload copy
register: Current Thread / original lock order / durable recheck
ready: Actual owner / join end / absolute deadline
transient: CV or I-O interruption abort
post: I-O postcheck / caller predicate or read retry
caller -> root: one capture before registration locks
root -> physical: same GC-repaired frame
physical -> service: install suffix without executing caller
service -> park: durable wait resumes
root -> park
park -> register
register -> physical: still pending
register -> ready: completed
ready -> caller: consuming physical restore
service -> transient: existing CV and I-O semantics
transient -> post
post -> caller
user: Retained full user continuation
service -> user: call/cc
user -> park: late multi-shot / current live Thread
baseline_control: Same C and four-way fxmul failure / no new arithmetic regression
measurement: matched compiled p1/p2 body latency and native peak
gap: OPEN downstream Gerbil / whole cold release admission
baseline_control -> gap: does not clear unexecuted cases
measurement -> gap: no whole speedup admission
gap -> register: historical SIGSEGV retained / current positives scoped { style.stroke-dash: 4 }
gc: Existing FrameSpec + forwarding + break handler
root -> gc
physical -> gc
user -> gc
word: Shared ordered word / ticket acquire and unlock release
message: GC payload / release stamp / acquire copy / reset
reverse: Reverse tree message / consumption before reuse
resources: VM-owned pair / per-slot construction bits
word -> register: queue ownership visibility
word -> message: same atomic interface
message -> gc: ordered operation payload
message -> reverse
reverse -> message: next fixed-tree payload
resources -> reverse: retained until closed VM and sender drain { style.stroke-dash: 4 }
slot: VM sync_constructed / partial native acquisition
reuse: Reset message state / retain mutex and CV
drain: Closed VM + joined carriers / dispose acquired bits
slot -> resources: once per physical slot
resources -> reuse: retirement retains native handles
reuse -> message: reverse-tree cut precedes payload reuse
resources -> drain: no child destruction
priority: Frozen owner graph / key change and queue lease
priority -> register: whole graph source candidate / cyclic admission open { style.stroke-dash: 4 }
record: Scheme priority-update STRUCTURE / ticket + scratch + roots
record -> priority: correct tagged-object ABI
record -> gc: ordinary roots / allocation before lease
ownerDebt: Historical cyclic GC counterexample
modelDebt: Existing QNT custody / least closure / finite key laws
ownerDebt -> priority_solve: excludes iterative convergence
modelDebt -> ownerDebt: temporal duty / not a native witness
caseLedger: Python source and terminal validators
caseLedger -> priority: real p1 and p2 checks
caseLedger -> ownerDebt: scoped passes do not close this duty
admission: ASCENT required-acceptance veto
ownerDebt -> admission: blocks whole result
caseLedger -> admission: source-bound facts
evidence: Registered Python Evidence view / checked references
identity: Candidate tree + runtime artifacts + profile observation
working: Changed working sources / unqualified
evidence -> identity: ASCENT shared Library
evidence -> priority: source and scoped native facts / no whole admission
working -> evidence: stale reference rejects query

frontend: Unadmitted frontend / macro capability closure open
compilerTask: Existing gxc invoke / physical output claim
completion: Successful native return / output + MD reads
quiescence: Parent reaped / group quiescent
completionJournal: Existing Evidence journal / header + runId
reuseTask: Same argv cwd source provider headers output
frontend -> compilerTask
compilerTask -> completion
completion -> quiescence
quiescence -> completionJournal
completionJournal -> reuseTask: immutable witness before derived cache
reuseTask -> compilerTask: changed identity executes

module_program: "Complete module program"
module_program -> native_completion: "Actual child return and all metadata writers"
module_program -> dependency_frontier: "Exact imported cohort, closed under dependencies"
dependency_frontier -> ready_interface: "Journal + stable bytes + quiescent parent"
ready_interface -> downstream: "Actual macro consumer imports same lexical cohort"

global_addressability: "Native global addressability: 12196 -> 20000"
ready_interface -> global_addressability: "Compiled phase loading"
global_addressability -> downstream: "Historical failure at unchanged capacity"

historical_identity -> global_addressability: "Historical eager SSI identity query" { style.stroke-dash: 4 }
module_program -> metadata_graph: "Admitted identity and dependency metadata"
make_identity -> reader_identity: "No admitted program"
reader_identity: Header reader / no body expansion
reader_identity -> metadata_graph: "Ordinary Scheme identity only"
metadata_graph -> frontend: "Needs generation: original macro discovery"
metadata_graph -> downstream: "Existing Make completion edges, without phase activation"

metadata_query: "Checked identity / dependency metadata"
macro_activation: "Actual compilation owns phase activation"
native_module: "Module-owned requests / original gxc quota"
private_ssi: "Private SSI until all native jobs join"
module_witness: "Complete outputs / stable dependencies / quiescent parent"
metadata_query -> macro_activation: "only when compilation needs it"
macro_activation -> native_module
native_module -> private_ssi: "drain success"
private_ssi -> module_witness
module_witness -> metadata_query: "next incremental build"

compiler_unit: "Physical unit plan: source and scoped native pass; whole consumers OPEN"
compiler_profile: "Original profile: unlimited single host"
compiler_variant: "Historical multiple-host flag diagnostic: no producer admission"
compiler_unit -> native_module: "source-owned plan; whole consumers still required"
compiler_profile -> compiler_unit
compiler_variant -> compiler_unit: "counterfactual, not acceptance"

compiler_phase_audit: {
 label: "Observed compiler boundaries; no stage-reuse admission"
 managedEmission: "Closed Gerbil emission bundle before native task drain\nExplicit-argument real-GSC lifecycle controls pass. Actual stdlib histories expose repeated coordinator activation before four generation resumes; the coordinator now has a planning-only prefix path. The installed reader/coordinator passes3 actual issued payloads and192 native cases with ordered dependency waits and forbidden import/completion callbacks. Complete downstream replay remains required"
 generation: "GSC Scheme-to-C generation\nC retained; no successful reusable generation-stage receipt"
 semanticGraph: "Semantic context graph capture\nActual generated .init outputs observed; codec256 and three real source/SSI comparisons pass. Cold new cohort and its continuation remain failed parents; individually witnessed complete programs retain graph custody."
 initializerProjection: "Pure initializer graph projection and slot view\nNative256 projection/alias/phase/GC/cycle controls and three real source/SSI comparisons pass. Installed119-root planning completes161 entries in3.113309s with native global cells18042 unchanged. Raw full-graph/class reconstruction controls time out at30s and remain failed."
 cFrontend: "C preprocessing and parsing\nOriginal-layout syntax-only control passes8.640044s; preprocessing reports2.93s"
 nativeConstruction: "Full C-to-module construction, including its frontend\nCurrent d07/987c59dd completes740 static units and all four original Make consumers; historical1b/7308 remains a separate source period. Pure Scheme generation chooses per-procedure physical hosts; embedded-C retains configured layout. Current ca_dr first observed C pair differs only by HOST_LAYOUT declaration. Isolated30s native compilation is censored in both roles; current-header u16vector layout variants both compile and pass. Do not infer all77 coverage losses or a universal host-layout speedup from this control."
 settlement: "Module job drain, private SSI publication and whole-module witness\nCurrent d07f67b4/987c59dd ABI326 complete stdlib programs,740 static native units and natural stdlib/libgerbil/lang/tools exits. Prior partial/failed parents retain separate source periods and completion prefixes. Complete cost/coverage attribution remains a different gate."
 libraryOrder: "Library runtime dependency ordering before static compilation\nCurrent d07f67b4/987c59dd consumes326 complete program graphs and326 compact views; original stdlib/libgerbil/lang/tools all naturally exit under unchanged limits. Current incremental stage times15.974612/46.084959/8.684437/94.919886s;740 static units complete,686 reused and54 executed in the closing library attempt. Historical1b/7308 measurements remain distinct. Tools registration pressure is resolved by the real VM-storage/root-index separation, not a raised capacity. Historical119-root/58fe43 planning and20000-limit failures remain documentary controls. This is not a cold matched build or4/4 release admission."
 generation -> semanticGraph: "After actual meta-code generation, capture getter-visible context identity, prelude/import/export/set edges and signed phases without changing emitted code"
 semanticGraph -> settlement: "Registered .init writer and exact bytes remain owned alongside pending SSI/native tasks. Failed generation may retain only a closed generation continuation. Native drain and quiescent completion precede graph-ready issuance"
 settlement -> initializerProjection: "Original semantic graph remains bound to a coherent native/interface program; projection may issue only its own data result with input/contract/output identities"
 initializerProjection -> libraryOrder: "Issue typed initialization-view transport only after closed data derivation; library uses its original traversal with pure slot getters, preserving context identity, phase edges and active cycles"
 managedEmission -> generation: "Only source-bound closed generation witnesses may supply planning identity/dependencies before the original worker restores immutable code and private SSI into the same managed program. The coordinator always enqueues this work and never posts module completion for a generation prefix. Original native argv and CPU quota remain. All native work must succeed and source/dependency identities must still match before public SSI publication"
 settlement -> libraryOrder: "Verified complete stdlib modules may supply stable interface identities. Their all-phase reuse dependency list does not authorize a phase-0 ordered link plan or public library completion"
 generation -> cFrontend: "Stable generated tokens and complete producer input cut; diagnostic retained-file access does not issue reuse"
 nativeConstruction -> settlement: "Every owned native request succeeds under the required profile; unknown or timed-out output retains custody and cannot publish"
}
globalIdentity: {
 label: "globalIdentity"
 tooltip: "Shared monotonic identity in the existing int domain. Identity publication does not allocate a dense slot in every live VM. The20000 backing-array admission rule retires, without raising heap/profile capacity options."
}
vmGlobals: {
 label: "vmGlobals"
 tooltip: "One VM-owned store. One page holds WORD_WIDTH ordinary and primitive cells plus one primitive-presence word. Page/cell addresses remain stable. A half-full append-only directory doubles geometrically; old directories remain VM-owned until the existing cleanup permit. Reads allocate nothing; binding prepares cells before generated writes."
}
frozenGlobals: {
 label: "frozenGlobals"
 tooltip: "After writer closure, capture this VM's page head/count once. Partition dense page ordinals, never shared identity count. Both standalone and whole-round publishers initialize each shard cursor. RootTask owns ordinary cells and active primitive overrides in its exact page range. Scan metadata is not a Scheme root. No page/directory is reclaimed until VM cleanup admits all readers and tasks drained."
}
globalRead: {
 label: "globalRead"
 tooltip: "Runtime and native ordered-word generated modules share one outlined address resolver. The exported service remains an ABI adapter; legacy/emulated generated targets retain that service. Preserve acquire loads, collision traversal, stable VM cell lifetime and fresh mutable payload loads. No address/value cache, purity annotation, allocation, poll, callback or layout change. Existing GC/cleanup ownership and QNT/Lean premises are unchanged. Native timing variation and lookup overhead remain empirical costs, not proven gains."
}
globalIdentity -> vmGlobals: "Binding transaction maps stable identity to VM storage before symbol/module publication; allocator failure leaves identity unpublished or retains existing binding responsibility."
vmGlobals -> frozenGlobals: "Existing RC writer closure and global_gate publish one immutable page inventory; main-round and standalone adapters must refine the same cursor/range contract."
vmGlobals -> globalRead: "An acquired immutable directory denotes initialized stable pages through the VM cleanup permit; a read never prepares missing storage or retains a borrowed cell past VM lifetime."
static_unit_custody: {
 label: "Per-unit native result custody"
 tooltip: "The original libgerbil work group produces370 Scheme-to-C and370 C-to-object units. A typed nine-field request identifies context, role, program, argv, cwd, source, source blob, output and contract. Existing process-status and close establish result custody; immutable completion plus stable source/header identities establish reuse. Batch failure retains independently closed units but cannot issue parent completion. Existing incremental_build.qnt start/finish/publish/reuse owns the temporal distinction; no new Lean temporal obligation is introduced."
}
compiler_phase_audit.nativeConstruction -> static_unit_custody
compiler_service_readiness: {
 label: "Same-source compiler service readiness"
 tooltip: "The same driver source may become one original gxc-produced native service. Input stability, output alias exclusion, quiescent original producer, immutable journal custody and a real native module/protocol smoke are all required before publishing its ready transport. Source loading remains the bootstrap path. Host-role and downstream-role classification must precede effective input equality; observing target-output changes does not authorize relabeling products. Both gxc and child GSC must use the existing p1 profile because original run.sh replaces GAMBOPT. Readiness and whole downstream admission are separate."
}
compiler_phase_audit.nativeConstruction -> compiler_service_readiness
compiler_service_readiness -> compiler_phase_audit.libraryOrder
physical_unit_plan: "A GVM procedure in a unit without module-level C interfaces owns one physical C host; the module retains one translation unit for shared constants, bindings and initialization. Inline c-code still uses its existing local primitive contract; this classification does not prove absence of C or side effects. A large procedure and whole-unit preprocessing remain unbounded"
compiler_phase_audit.generation -> physical_unit_plan: "post-scan plan"
physical_unit_plan -> compiler_phase_audit.nativeConstruction: "producer-owned host declaration; original profile"
closure_ownerFlow: "OWNED-CONTROL\nSCOPED_QUALIFIED"
closure_consumerChain: "CURRENT-CONSUMERS\nCLOSED_NATIVE"
closure_budgetCause: "COVERAGE-CAUSE\nCLOSED_MATCHED_CASE_REVIEW"
closure_releasePopulation: "MATCHED-COST\nCLOSED_DECLARED_POPULATION"
closure_revisionAdmission: "REV-ADMISSION\nOPEN_FIVE_GATES"
closure_ownerFlow -> closure_revisionAdmission: "Managed semantic/source and native duties remain qualified on the final source."
closure_consumerChain -> closure_revisionAdmission: "Actual current-ABI natural consumer exits; failed parents retain their status."
closure_budgetCause -> closure_revisionAdmission: "Attribute77 unmatched completions before declaring the deficit harmless."
closure_releasePopulation -> closure_revisionAdmission: "Declared matched cost population and explicit overhead disposition, not an inferred universal speedup."
delivery_boundary: "SysML frozen delivery scope / exact declared dependency population"
delivery_boundary -> closure_ownerFlow: "classify within reviewed scope"
delivery_boundary -> closure_consumerChain: "classify within reviewed scope"
delivery_boundary -> closure_budgetCause: "classify within reviewed scope"
